{"title":"Brahmagupta's Identity","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Brahmagupta's identity</b> states that for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fb3e225fc42b4d870d34247558a9bbf324931fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d, n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/1/63196b276a64199ae4bd0ec5d8b8c847fe18dc24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (a^2+nb^2)(c^2+nd^2) &amp;= (ac+nbd)^2 + n(ad-bc)^2 \\\\ &amp;= (ac-nbd)^2 + n(ad+bc)^2. \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"386\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the product of two integers that can both be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/9249829396b3c85b63681e2dd0159f73c09c2cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + ny^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" /> for a given integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can be written in the same form for the same value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Brahmagupta%27s_Identity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We expand the left side:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8ea54116bbbf1d8089fa7819f89a9567e20ced9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (a^2+nb^2)(c^2+nd^2) &amp;= a^2c^2 + na^2d^2 + nb^2c^2 + n^2b^2d^2 \\\\ &amp;= (ac)^2 + (nbd)^2 + n(ad)^2 + n(bc)^2. \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"440\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Adding and then subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7eba809c9efa92c1f63d0696b39140bef74d0612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2nabcd$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> to the result yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/2/102457d5da0b79610a5eb6022764d538d11f6b5f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} (ac)^2 + 2(ac)(nbd) + (nbd)^2 + n(ad)^2 - 2n(ad)(bc) + n(bc)^2 \\\\ = (ac+nbd)^2 + n(ad-bc)^2, \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"463\" height=\"47\" /> while subtracting and then adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7eba809c9efa92c1f63d0696b39140bef74d0612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2nabcd$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c029b4b9d062b3bebfa7c888969928308814a4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} (ac)^2 - 2(ac)(nbd) + (nbd)^2 + n(ad)^2 + 2n(ad)(bc) + n(bc)^2 \\\\ = (ac-nbd)^2 + n(ad+bc)^2. \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"463\" height=\"47\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Application_to_the_Pell_equation\">Application to the Pell equation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Brahmagupta%27s_Identity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Application to the Pell equation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffa1b27ebc52376a62c3b1c78e7a88ebf1202a7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = -D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" />, the forms involved in Brahmagupta's identity lend themselves to use with solutions to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell_equation\" title=\"Pell equation\">Pell equation</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a63ba10d806de46ab8e674925e840639bba1814.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 - Dy^2 = 1.\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Composition_of_solutions\">Composition of solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Brahmagupta%27s_Identity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Composition of solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e31171b9eaf222673b566ed3cf773e0f0b532c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> are both solution pairs to the Pell equation for a given value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54f160e6c6dbd80ba81cc75c9ee181a1a5e7ed09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(ac-Dbd)^2 - D(ad-bc)^2 = (a^2-Db^2)(c^2-Dd^2) = 1 \\cdot 1 = 1,\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"20\" /> and likewise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d6c6967d7b9420fa7ec6721549d90655ae2c07.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(ac+Dbd)^2 - D(ad+bc)^2 = (a^2-Db^2)(c^2-Dd^2) = 1.\\]\" width=\"438\" height=\"20\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/c/78c25935b5d30f981a8c6eb6cd2523eb042a6359.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ac-Dbd, ad-bc)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/b/fab7476451758379cb0f34a34ec92701919fba72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ac+Dbd, ad+bc)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" /> are two (not necessarily distinct) solutions to the same equation.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018074832\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.025 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 91/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3803/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24038:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018074832 and revision id 190513. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}